# For AI Agent

> Copy this into your project's `AGENTS.md` and adjust the rules. `CLAUDE.md` imports it
> with one line: `@AGENTS.md`.
> Only rules that always apply belong here. How to use the tools is in the skills,
> which load when a request needs them.

## Memory Tool

- At the start of a session, read `.claude/memory-context.md`. If it is missing or stale, run `mcontext`.
- Record to the timeline only with `m`. Never create or edit timeline files by hand.
- When to record: at natural breakpoints. Finish the work, show the result, then ask whether to record it. *(Change this line to suit the project, for example "record every attempt and failure".)*
- Before answering a question about past work, search with `ms`. Do not guess.
- Small decisions go in the timeline. Write a document only for what someone will look up or need explained later.
- The knowledge base folder is not always `.memory/`. Run `mbase show` instead of assuming a path.

How to do each of these: the `mt-record` skill. Writing documents: `mt-write`. Publishing to the knowledge base: `mt-publish`.

